          "source_quote": "λοιπὸν δὲ περιλείπεται δεῖξαι αὐτοῖς πῶς πιστεύομεν ὅτι· θεῖον ἔχει πνεῦμα.",
          "english_quote": "It remains for them to show how we are to believe that it has a divine spirit.",
          "issue": "The main rendering is contextually defensible, but the note does not preserve the material alternative attachment of αὐτοῖς as the recipient of δεῖξαι: “to show them,” rather than “for them to show.” The existing alternative “how we believe” addresses πῶς πιστεύομεν, not this change in responsibility for demonstrating the claim.",
          "suggested_revision": "Expand the source-quoted note to preserve “to show them” as the alternative dative attachment. Explain why the main text instead takes αὐτοῖς with the impersonal construction as identifying the party responsible for demonstrating the claim, and retain the disclosed uncertainty concerning πῶς πιστεύομεν. This does not require correcting the verified print.",
          "severity": "major"
        },
        {
          "source_quote": "ἀλλ’ ἐπιδεῖξαι ἡμῖν οὐ δύναται ὅτι ἔστιν, ἐπεὶ μὴ ἔστιν — καὶ αὐτοῖς ἑωρακέναι οὐ πιστεύομεν.",
          "english_quote": "Yet they cannot demonstrate to us that it exists, since it does not—and we do not believe that they have seen it themselves.",
          "issue": "The draft supplies the worshipers as the subject of “cannot demonstrate,” but δύναται is singular and its subject is unstated. A representative individual opponent is a defensible contextual reading; an image or the alleged spirit is another possible subject. The notes do not disclose this material uncertainty about who or what cannot demonstrate existence.",
          "suggested_revision": "Add a source-quoted note identifying the singular δύναται and explaining the representative-opponent reading behind English “they.” Preserve the alternative “it cannot demonstrate to us that it exists,” with an image or the alleged spirit as subject. Do not treat the confirmed singular as an OCR error or silently regularize it.",
          "severity": "major"
        }
      ]
    },
