          "english_quote": "We should understand something similar about the gods that are stolen and despoiled.",
          "issue": "ἔστιν ἡμῖν νοεῖν expresses the possibility or availability of understanding the analogous situation. “Should” changes this into a recommendation or directive, rather than preserving the source’s modal expression.",
          "suggested_revision": "Use “We can understand something similar about the gods that are stolen and despoiled.”",
